และเครือข่ายคนจีนกำลังแปรเป็นสถาบันของชุมชน": "The surviving building was constructed in 1922 (พ.ศ. 2465) with funds 
collected from mining magnates and Chinese merchants in the old market at Yan Yao, as well as merchant networks from 
Ranong and Phuket. Another official source describes it as the work of a Chinese merchants' association that entered 
the tin-mining industry to provide Chinese-language education for Chinese children. The adapted Sino-Portuguese 
building with its corrugated-metal roof was therefore not only a school, but evidence that wealth from mining, trade, 
and Chinese networks was becoming a community institution.",
